# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Upstox PR Automation Platform - Environment Configuration
# Based on N8n workflow analysis - see N8N_WORKFLOW_ANALYSIS.md for details
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# ============================================================================
# BITBUCKET CONFIGURATION
# ============================================================================
# Base URL of your Bitbucket Server/Data Center instance
# Example: https://bitbucket.upstox.com
BITBUCKET_BASE_URL=https://your-bitbucket-domain.com

# Bitbucket username for API access
BITBUCKET_USERNAME=your-username

# Bitbucket app password or personal access token
# Create at: Bitbucket → Settings → Personal access tokens
BITBUCKET_APP_PASSWORD=your-app-password

# Maximum number of commits to fetch per PR (N8n default: 100)
BITBUCKET_COMMIT_LIMIT=100

# ============================================================================
# AI CONFIGURATION (Groq or OpenAI)
# ============================================================================
# AI Provider: 'groq' or 'openai'
AI_PROVIDER=groq

# API Key for the selected provider
# Groq: Get from https://console.groq.com/
# OpenAI: Get from https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
AI_API_KEY=your-api-key

# AI Model to use
# Groq models (from N8n workflows): openai/gpt-oss-120b, mixtral-8x7b-32768, llama-3.1-70b-versatile
# OpenAI models: gpt-4-turbo-preview, gpt-4, gpt-3.5-turbo
AI_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# AI Model Parameters (N8n defaults)
AI_TEMPERATURE=1
AI_MAX_TOKENS=8192
AI_TOP_P=1
AI_REASONING_EFFORT=medium

# ============================================================================
# SLACK CONFIGURATION
# ============================================================================
# Slack Incoming Webhook URL
# Create at: https://api.slack.com/messaging/webhooks
SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/YOUR/WEBHOOK/URL

# Default Slack channel for notifications (optional)
SLACK_DEFAULT_CHANNEL=#pr-reviews

# Maximum length of a single Slack message before chunking (N8n default: 2800)
SLACK_MESSAGE_MAX_LENGTH=2800

# Wait time (in milliseconds) between Slack posts to avoid rate limiting (N8n default: 2000)
SLACK_WAIT_BETWEEN_POSTS=2000

# ============================================================================
# PR REVIEW PROCESSING CONFIGURATION
# ============================================================================
# Number of files to include in each batch for AI review (N8n default: 2)
# Lower number = more focused reviews, but more API calls
REVIEW_FILES_PER_BATCH=2

# Number of context lines to include in diff for reviews (N8n default: 5)
REVIEW_CONTEXT_LINES=5

# Maximum number of recent commits to include in review context (N8n default: 10)
REVIEW_MAX_COMMITS=10

# Maximum characters per line in review output (N8n default: 120)
REVIEW_LINE_LENGTH_LIMIT=120

# Number of concurrent batch processing operations (N8n default: 3)
BATCH_CONCURRENCY=3

# ============================================================================
# PR DESCRIPTION GENERATION CONFIGURATION
# ============================================================================
# Number of context lines to include in diff for descriptions (N8n default: 3)
# Less context needed for descriptions vs reviews
DESCRIPTION_CONTEXT_LINES=3

# Minimum description length to consider PR "has description" (N8n default: 10)
# PRs with descriptions shorter than this will be processed
DESCRIPTION_MIN_LENGTH=10

# Maximum number of commits to include in description prompt (N8n default: 10)
DESCRIPTION_MAX_COMMITS=10

# Maximum number of key changes (added/removed lines) to show per file (N8n default: 5)
DESCRIPTION_MAX_KEY_CHANGES=5

# Maximum characters for key change lines (N8n default: 150)
DESCRIPTION_LINE_LENGTH_LIMIT=150

# Maximum characters for commit messages in description (N8n default: 80)
DESCRIPTION_COMMIT_LENGTH_LIMIT=80

# Number of top modified files to include in description (N8n default: 10)
DESCRIPTION_TOP_MODIFIED_FILES=10

# Author email to filter PRs for description generation
# Example: haneef.shaik@rksv.in (from N8n workflow)
# Only PRs authored by this user will get auto-generated descriptions
PR_DESCRIPTION_AUTHOR_EMAIL=your-email@example.com

# Cron expression for PR description generation (N8n default: every 10 minutes)
# Format: minute hour day month weekday
# Examples:
#   */10 * * * * = Every 10 minutes
#   */15 * * * * = Every 15 minutes
#   0 * * * * = Every hour
#   0 9-17 * * 1-5 = Every hour from 9 AM to 5 PM, Monday to Friday
CRON_PR_DESCRIPTION_INTERVAL=*/10 * * * *

# ============================================================================
# REPOSITORY CONFIGURATION
# ============================================================================
# Comma-separated list of repositories to process (format: PROJECT/REPO)
# Example from N8n workflow:
# GROWTH/ui-upstox-ipo,GROWTH/ui-stock-details,GROWTH/ui-trade-price-verification-tool
REPOS_WHITELIST=PROJECT1/repo1,PROJECT2/repo2

# Comma-separated list of repositories to exclude (optional)
REPOS_BLACKLIST=

# ============================================================================
# CRON JOB CONFIGURATION
# ============================================================================
# Secret token for authenticating cron job requests (optional but recommended)
# Generate a random string: openssl rand -hex 32
CRON_SECRET=your-random-secret-token

# Repository whitelist for cron job (JSON array format)
# Only these repositories will be processed by the scheduled cron job
# Example: [{"project":"GROWTH","repo":"ui-stock-details"},{"project":"GROWTH","repo":"ui-upstox-ipo"}]
CRON_REPO_WHITELIST=[{"project":"PROJECT","repo":"repo-name"}]

# Author filter for cron job (optional)
# Only PRs by this author will get auto-generated descriptions
# Example: John Doe
CRON_AUTHOR_FILTER=

# ============================================================================
# NEXT.JS CONFIGURATION (Optional)
# ============================================================================
# Public URL of the application (for deployment)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://your-domain.com

# Node environment
# NODE_ENV=production

# ============================================================================
# NOTES
# ============================================================================
# - All N8n workflow constants have been preserved with their original values
# - Review the N8N_WORKFLOW_ANALYSIS.md file for detailed explanations
# - Required variables: BITBUCKET_*, AI_*, SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL
# - Recommended: PR_DESCRIPTION_AUTHOR_EMAIL, REPOS_WHITELIST
# - Optional: All other settings have sensible defaults from N8n workflows
